	(text_box "Get rid of the INA190 because we have a span error greater than XTR200(0.001%) which would be 0.1% + 0.2%, resistor + INA190 respectivly.\nResistors are the main culprit of the error but since the DAC's internal reference has a span error of 0.2% for this design it's okay to go with 0.1% resistors\nThe ADC has a measurement span error of max 0.15% so the total error while reading voltage can be 0.2% + 0.15% = 0.35%\nOne option is to use RES11A-Q1\nWe use the DAC's internal reference to compensate for ADC's internal reference which drifts at 7ppm/C vs DAC at 2ppm/C\nUse ratiometric calibration \nWe only have to values current so add a MOSFET to switch between both values in the next version\nGet rid of precision resistors because of cost and supplier variablity\nEven for range switch use these\nAutoranging of ADS1118 can get laggy shifting to ADS1220\nRepick a DAC\nADC no daisy chain so individual CS pin use I2C expander\nDAC has daisy chain so one CS pin\nIf the ADC is accurate enough we measure the resistance of the TiN heater and use that as a temperature sensor"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 278.13 21.59 0)
		(size 127 86.36)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type dash)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6f786e91-16ae-4bf5-9b07-34c8c011c70e")
	)
	(text_box "ADS1220"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 356.87 190.5 0)
		(size 12.7 48.26)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
